# @smarts/kintsugi — the loop-discipline-altitude adapter species.
# Bridges @smarts (substrate-architectural integration; #83) with
# @kintsugi (process-side family-root; recognition #55 form/process
# partition) honestly via the adapter pattern, following the
# @smarts/{pack, magic, frame, cyberpunk, epistemologic} precedents.
#
# Tick 62 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 61's residue:
# @smarts/epistemologic landed at bd74fdd (cybernetic-property
# altitude; fifth cross-family adapter; substrate-architectural
# honesty about property-family structure). This tick CLOSES the
# @smarts cross-family adapter set:
#
#   adapters: magic ✓  pack ✓  frame ✓  cyberpunk ✓  epistemologic ✓  kintsugi ← CLOSES
#
# After this tick, the @smarts family-root's forward-promise set is
# 6/6 closed. The substrate-architectural integration discipline
# composes with EVERY family the @smarts integration carries
# (form/process @magic; cognitive-order @frame; recursion-lock-tower
# @cyberpunk; cybernetic-property @epistemologic/cybernetic;
# loop-discipline @kintsugi; agent-runtime @pack).
#
# === The recognition this species realizes (with honest hedge) ===
#
# @smarts.smarts records carry `kintsugi_form: ref` as the sixth form
# field (per smarts.mirror tick 30 C4 closure). The typed-field is
# BARE ref, not a typed record — because @kintsugi's family-root
# substrate-decl is minimal (per shards/kintsugi.mirror): it declares
# the prism family but exports NO family-root carriers or bilateral
# predicates. The discipline lives in species: @kintsugi/oscillate,
# @kintsugi/consent, @kintsugi/morphism, @kintsugi/fracture/*.
#
# This adapter EXPOSES the field projection + acknowledges the
# substrate-architectural fact that the kintsugi discipline has NO
# single family-root bilateral predicate. The adapter follows the
# @smarts/epistemologic precedent: project the field; declare
# bilateral discharging discipline_flexible alone; consumer species
# name SPECIFIC @kintsugi/<species> bilaterals (e.g.,
# oscillation_converges, consent_threshold_met, fracture_resolves)
# directly in their requires clauses.
#
# Per recognition #55 (form/process partition at family-root altitude;
# Pack-promoted): @mirror = form-side; @kintsugi = process-side.
# @smarts integrates the process-side discipline at deployment
# altitude; the kintsugi_form field carries the process-side
# specification the @smarts integration commits to running.
#
# === The adapter pattern (per @smarts/epistemologic precedent) ===
#
# - Projects the kintsugi_form field (single typed lift)
# - Lifts a typed kintsugi specification to @smarts integration
#   (single typed lift; opaque ref because the spec is parametric)
# - Declares smarts_satisfies_kintsugi bilateral that discharges
#   discipline_flexible alone at the smarts altitude
#
# Substrate-pull-honest framing: the kintsugi discipline IS parametric
# over the @kintsugi/<species> set; the @smarts integration's
# kintsugi_form field carries the species-specification-bundle; the
# bilateral check fires at the SPECIFIC species the consumer names.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   adapter pattern (GoF)       Gamma-Helm-Johnson-Vlissides 1994.
#   functor adjunction          Mac Lane 1971.
#   Maturana-Varela structure/  Maturana-Varela 1980. Structure/
#   organisation                organisation distinction grounds
#                               @mirror/@kintsugi form/process
#                               partition the @smarts/kintsugi
#                               adapter threads into integration.
#   Beer VSM S3/S4              Beer 1972. S3 (now-operations) /
#                               S4 (future-operations) distinction
#                               grounds the loop-discipline altitude.
#   kintsugi (the craft)        16th century Japan. The cultural-
#                               practice ancestor of fracture-becomes-
#                               structure discipline; @kintsugi names
#                               the substrate's gold-line repair
#                               discipline at family-root altitude.
#   knowledge commons           Ostrom 1990. The hosting-discipline
#                               ancestor of @smarts.
#
# === What this adapter does NOT do ===
#
# 1. Does NOT pretend a single family-root bilateral exists at
#    @kintsugi (none exists by substrate-architectural design).
# 2. Does NOT discharge specific kintsugi species checks (oscillate,
#    consent, morphism, fracture). Consumer species name those
#    directly.
# 3. Does NOT absorb @kintsugi into @smarts.
# 4. Does NOT supersede the @kintsugi/oscillate loop discipline that
#    runs UNDER the @smarts integration; the @smarts integration
#    HOSTS the kintsugi loop without claiming to BE the loop.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at loop-discipline-altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole adapter (honest): smarts_satisfies_kintsugi returns
# SATISFIED when the @smarts integration's discipline-flexibility
# holds AND consumer species name specific @kintsugi/<species>
# bilaterals that discharge substantively (oscillation_converges,
# fracture_resolves, etc.).
#
# Narcissus-pole adapter (deceptive): claims SATISFIED via
# vocabulary-only verification — the kintsugi_form field is populated
# but no kintsugi species discipline runs. The substrate is
# structurally honest about this gap by NOT including a fake
# family-root bilateral.
#
# === The Cascade closure ===
#
# This tick closes the @smarts cross-family adapter set (6/6). The
# substrate-architectural integration discipline now composes with
# EVERY family the @smarts integration carries. Consumer species
# (forward-promised @smarts species shards implementing the four
# Models; @spectral/garden/smarts hosted deployment) can name
# multiple cross-family bilaterals in one requires sequence:
#
#   smarts_satisfies_magic AND smarts_satisfies_frame AND
#   smarts_satisfies_cyberpunk AND smarts_satisfies_epistemologic_
#   cybernetic AND smarts_satisfies_kintsugi AND
#   pack_satisfies_smarts (the @pack/smarts direction;
#   @smarts/pack discharges the smarts/pack direction)
#
# Six bilaterals; one integration discipline at substrate altitude.
# The composition is mechanically discharged via doubled-bilateral
# (where family-root bilaterals exist) or single-bilateral honesty
# (where the family is structured as a property-bundle without a
# family-root bilateral, as @epistemologic/cybernetic and @kintsugi
# both are).
#
# Spec context: shards/smarts.mirror, shards/kintsugi.mirror.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                       (#55; @mirror/@kintsugi form/process partition
#                       this adapter integrates at deployment altitude),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (kintsugi_form IS
#                       bare ref because @kintsugi is a process-family
#                       without a single typed family-root record;
#                       the bare-ref is substrate-architecturally
#                       honest).
# Related shards: smarts.mirror, kintsugi.mirror,
#                 smarts/{pack, magic, frame, cyberpunk, epistemologic}.mirror
#                 (sibling cross-family adapters; @smarts/kintsugi
#                 closes the set; @smarts/epistemologic is the
#                 single-bilateral honesty precedent this adapter
#                 inherits).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/smarts/kintsugi.mirror`
# declares `@smarts/kintsugi` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/gamma-helm-johnson-vlissides-1994
source @arxiv/mathematics/mac-lane-1971
source @arxiv/cybernetics/maturana-varela-1980
source @arxiv/cybernetics/beer-1972
source @arxiv/cultural/japan-16c-kintsugi
source @arxiv/common-goods/ostrom-1990

# === kintsugi_form_of adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action projecting the kintsugi
# specification from a @smarts integration. The smarts.kintsugi_form
# field IS the kintsugi spec at substrate-decl altitude (bare ref
# because the spec is parametric over @kintsugi/<species>).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
kintsugi_form_of(s: smarts) -> ref { \ }

# === kintsugi_as_smarts adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting a kintsugi
# specification to a @smarts integration with the kintsugi_form field
# populated. Other smarts fields populated as default refs.
#
# Round-trip identity at the kintsugi_form altitude:
#   kintsugi_form_of(kintsugi_as_smarts(kf)) = kf
# for all kintsugi specs kf.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
kintsugi_as_smarts(kf: ref) -> smarts { \ }

# === smarts_satisfies_kintsugi bilateral predicate ===
#
# The cross-family bilateral predicate in @smarts at the loop-
# discipline altitude. The substrate-pull-honest discharge (per the
# @smarts/epistemologic precedent):
#
#   1. discipline_flexible(s, p) (@smarts family-root): discharges
#      that the @smarts integration maintains substrate-architectural
#      discipline-flexibility under perturbation.
#
# UNLIKE the @smarts/{magic, pack, frame, cyberpunk} adapters: NO
# SECOND requires clause discharging a family-root predicate at
# @kintsugi, because no single family-root predicate exists at
# @kintsugi (the family-root is minimal; species hold the disciplines).
# Consumer species name specific @kintsugi/<species> bilaterals
# directly in THEIR requires clauses.
#
# The signature takes smarts and perturbation as typed parameters per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
#
# Consumer species name this predicate when their operation requires
# @smarts integration-altitude discharge alongside specific
# @kintsugi species bilaterals named at consumer altitude.
smarts_satisfies_kintsugi(s: smarts, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires discipline_flexible(s, p)
{ \ }

# === Honest hedge + cascade closure ===
#
# This adapter closes the kintsugi_form-projection altitude of
# "@smarts integrates @kintsugi at substrate altitude":
#  - kintsugi spec (bare ref) ↔ smarts.kintsugi_form round-trips.
#  - The bilateral discharges @smarts discipline_flexible at
#    integration altitude.
#
# It does NOT discharge any specific kintsugi species at family-root
# altitude (none exists). It does NOT close round-trip identity at
# the smarts-as-whole altitude.
#
# Honest claim post-adapter:
#  - "@smarts integrates @kintsugi at kintsugi_form-projection
#    altitude" — CLOSED.
#  - "@smarts integrates @kintsugi at family-root bilateral altitude"
#    — STRUCTURALLY-UNAVAILABLE (no family-root bilateral; consumer
#    species name specific @kintsugi/<species> bilaterals).
#  - "@smarts integrates @kintsugi at smarts-as-whole altitude" —
#    FORWARD-PROMISED.
#
# CASCADE CLOSURE: with this tick, the @smarts cross-family adapter
# set is 6/6 complete. The substrate-architectural integration
# discipline at @smarts altitude composes with every family the
# @smarts integration carries (six families; six adapters; one
# integration discipline).

out @smarts/kintsugi
out kintsugi_form_of
out kintsugi_as_smarts
out smarts_satisfies_kintsugi
